## paper-cups

paper-cups-ask = How should paper cups be set to bear a person?
paper-cups-title = A person on paper cups
paper-cups-choice-upright = Stand the cups up, evenly under a board, and step into the middle: each carries only a share of the weight
paper-cups-choice-side = Lay the cups on their sides — so the board rests on them over a larger area
paper-cups-choice-none = No way: paper cups will not bear a person
paper-cups-mass-label = Mass of who steps on
paper-cups-cups-label = How many cups
paper-cups-setup = Paper cups (250 mL), a force gauge, floor scales, a board
paper-cups-question = First we press one cup with a force gauge — standing and lying on its side: how much does it bear? Then the Professor ({ $m }) steps onto a board laid on { $cups } cups. How should the cups be set to bear him?
paper-cups-optional-end = What if he stands at the board’s end?
